From dc95c947f25fffdc5a50e9b489d830cc7dcf665e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 04:00:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): track kept observers across offline restore
 publication [daveey]

Problem: source-backup failure let unlink+move replace a board beneath a
real in-process cached_ro reader. Foreign scans skip self and the reader
joined only the generation WeakSet, not the offline holder registry.

Use the writer's lifecycle/guard/tracking factory order with nonblocking
registry admission, retaining the existing retry budget outside the board
lock. Preserve bytes paths and legacy positional sqlite options. Keep all
reader custody until real close/GC; never evict a borrower to permit a swap.

Also reserve missing-target import against kept deleted-inode readers.
Clear stale sidecars only after holder refusal/reservation, so a nonempty
old WAL cannot replay over the imported snapshot.

Detection: existing tracked-state/corrupt-header and foreign-process
fixtures did not cover real cached_ro with source-backup-only failure.
Add real public-wrapper refusal, retained observer and fd proof, missing
publication/stale WAL, lifetime/GC/close and deterministic race tests.

Proof: real idle cached_ro RED returns True with deleted target fd before
tracking. New missing-target RED publishes under kept observer and retains
stale WAL. Focused GREEN: 5 files, 30 tests. All fallback bytes and identities
unchanged from injected source backup failure; the prior live-safe TRUNCATE
checkpoint may refresh SHM salts/readmarks only within first 136 bytes.
Independent Opus design+addendum reviewed before each production change.
Correctness only: no G26 revival or performance acceptance.
